  "created_at": "2024-11-26T16:22:01Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-11-26T16:22:01Z",
  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nIt does not require a local nix store, it consumes nix store paths as input and tries to download the path and all its dependencies to the local filesystem from any given remote binary cache (defaults tocache.nixos.org). \r\n\r\nThis assumes that you already know the calculated store path, for this you need to have nix installed. You could use e.g. nix eval to get a store path: \r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ nix eval nixpkgs#hello.outPath\r\n\"/nix/store/041gszy7ccgmjv83lif6j6rzbqz5vjzg-hello-2.12.1\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd then you can pass this store path to `nix-download` on any other machine/container to download and run it.\r\n\r\nDoes this help?",
  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "pin": null,
